## [Legacy debt]($section.id('legacy-debt'))

### [Inherited debt does not absorb new failures]($section.id('inherited-debt-does-not-absorb-new-failures').attrs('verified'))

[baseline]($text.attrs('tag')) [regressions]($text.attrs('tag'))
[View test](https://github.com/benomahony/overwatch/blob/main/tests/acceptance/catalog.py#L102)

- [Given]($text.attrs('given')) [The session starts with 29 inherited warnings under the default policy](https://github.com/benomahony/overwatch/blob/main/tests/acceptance/world.py#L158).
- [When]($text.attrs('when')) [The agent attempts completion and publication](https://github.com/benomahony/overwatch/blob/main/tests/acceptance/world.py#L178).
- [Then]($text.attrs('then')) [Completion and configured publication actions are allowed](https://github.com/benomahony/overwatch/blob/main/tests/acceptance/world.py#L186).
- [When]($text.attrs('when')) [A change increases the warning count to 30](https://github.com/benomahony/overwatch/blob/main/tests/acceptance/world.py#L283).
- [Then]($text.attrs('then')) [The new failure guards completion](https://github.com/benomahony/overwatch/blob/main/tests/acceptance/world.py#L290).

### [A commit made with a failing edit does not hide the failure]($section.id('a-commit-made-with-a-failing-edit-does-not-hide-the-failure').attrs('verified'))

[baseline]($text.attrs('tag')) [regressions]($text.attrs('tag')) [commits]($text.attrs('tag'))
[View test](https://github.com/benomahony/overwatch/blob/main/tests/acceptance/catalog.py#L109)

- [Given]($text.attrs('given')) [The project's files are committed and the session starts with a passing check](https://github.com/benomahony/overwatch/blob/main/tests/acceptance/world.py#L307).
- [When]($text.attrs('when')) [One shell step breaks the check and commits the change](https://github.com/benomahony/overwatch/blob/main/tests/acceptance/world.py#L314).
- [Then]($text.attrs('then')) [The failure is reported as new and Stop is refused](https://github.com/benomahony/overwatch/blob/main/tests/acceptance/world.py#L322).

